WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.137
PRESENTER: Hi.

00:00:01.137 --> 00:00:02.970
Today we're going to
see how Document AI can

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.740
help unlock insights
from documents

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.150
with machine learning.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.920
Data is crucial in
helping businesses

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.460
make smart decisions.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.550
But today, much of that
valuable information

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.120
is dark data, stored in formats
that are difficult to analyze,

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.960
as handwritten forms,
PDFs, images, and emails.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.700
Companies in all
industries and sizes,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.100
from financial institutions
to media companies

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.040
to medical organizations,
face this challenge.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.590
That's where Document AI,
Google Cloud's solution

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.009
for understanding documents
like forms, IDs, and invoices

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:33.780
can help.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.300
Here's an example of what a
solution built with Document AI

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.350
might look like.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.810
Acme, a fictional dental
insurance company,

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.240
processes thousands
of claims each week.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.890
Previously, when
they received a form

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.840
from a dentist's
office or a patient,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.360
an Acme employee would
manually enter all of the claim

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.440
information into a database.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.990
This was tedious,
time consuming,

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.250
and lengthened the
claim's processing time.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.210
Thanks to Document AI, Acme
has automated the process

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:00.260
and reduced the average
time to close a claim.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.950
Now when a new
claim is received,

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.540
the form is uploaded to the
Acme dental claim portal.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.940
Next, the Document AI API
analyzes the claim and extracts

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.380
data from its fields,
like patient information,

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:14.790
procedure details, and
dentist authorization.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.590
After data is extracted
from the claim,

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.780
the Acme dental claim
portal automatically

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.030
stores it in a
BigQuery database.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:24.100
Acme can easily search,
browse, and analyze claim data,

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.620
allowing them to make
better business decisions.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.260
So how did Acme do it?

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.960
When a claim is uploaded, it's
sent to the Document AI API.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:33.780
This API uses a
specialized model

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.260
to understand form fields,
tables, and check boxes.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.270
Once data is extracted
from the application,

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.715
it's stored in BigQuery,
Google Cloud's data warehouse,

00:01:41.715 --> 00:01:44.160
where it can be queried,
allowing Acme to service

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.960
insights through their portal.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.640
Now Acme employees
can store claims

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.220
in a database, flag anomalies,
and make better business

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:53.880
decisions, faster, without the
burden of manual data input.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.520
To learn more about how Document
AI can help you gain insights

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.440
from your documents,
check out the Document AI

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.650
page on Cloud.Google.com,
and thanks for watching.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:06.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

